      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Annoyingly enough this also applies to bloom, so any green screen footage will end up being washed out with synthetic spill.\n\nRelatedly it would be nice if there were somehow some way for grab passes to still get the background from the world itself, so that glass-like materials work reasonably well, but that would probably be super difficult with the way that Unity shader passes work. Maybe render the world to one buffer and the avatars to another, and have the avatar buffer be cleared with transparent alpha first?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
